# Content packs (All-In-One)

Uni+ Learning Tools reads **only** `content-packs/` through content-api. A pack appears when this file exists:

`content-packs/<pack-folder>/manifest.json`

Do **not** nest packs in `S3/` or any year folder. Do **not** add teaching files under `public/`, `dist/`, `js/`, or `index.html` (old hub).

## Folder shape (one Layer 1 chapter = one pack)

Same naming as Physics (`ch1-heat-and-gases`): `ch` + chapter number + slug.

```
content-packs/ch01-earth/
  manifest.json
  quiz.json                 ← chapter quiz index
  notes/*.pdf
  tools/<slug>/index.html
  worksheets/<slug>/index.html
  quiz/<topic-slug>/quiz.json
  summaries/
```

Published S3 packs are `ch01-earth` (CPE01–CPE04) and `ch02-microscopic-world-i` (CMWA01–CMWA05). Later Excel chapters are `ch03-metal` through `ch15-analytical-chemistry`.

Do **not** create one pack per Layer 2 topic (`01-fundamentals-of-chemistry`).

## New chapter

1. Copy an existing pack folder. Rename it from the Excel Layer 1 chapter (`ch03-metal`).
2. In `manifest.json`: `subject` `"CHEM"`, unique lowercase `scope` (`earth`, `metal`), `chapterCode` (`CH01`), `published: true`.
3. Set `title.en` to the chapter name without the code (`Earth`) so Learning Tools shows **CH01 Earth**.
4. Keep `packId`, `subject`, `scope`, `title`, and `published` in `manifest.json`. Learning Tools also scans the chapter folder: `notes/*.pdf` and `*/<slug>/index.html`. Manifest entries still win for titles and topic codes.

## New item inside a chapter

Add a note PDF under `notes/` (`CPE01-….pdf`). Add labs and flashcard pages under `tools/<slug>/index.html`. Put worksheets under `worksheets/<slug>/` (not inside `tools/`). Put a game under `games/<slug>/` or keep it in `tools/` with `"section": "games"`. A new kebab-case folder of HTML tools (for example `lab-sheets/<slug>/index.html`) becomes its own Learning Tools tab. List items in `tools` when you need a title or topic code; unlisted HTML still publishes. Tag listed items with a **Topic Code** from `content/topics/chem-topics.json`. Do not invent codes.

## Quizzes

List quiz info in two places, same as S3 Physics:

1. Chapter `quiz.json` — index of every topic quiz in that pack.
2. `quiz/<topic-slug>/quiz.json` — the items for that topic (`quizId`, `topicCode`, `items`).

Also list each topic in `manifest.json` `quiz[]` with `slug`, `quizId`, `topicCode`, `path`, and `file` pointing at that topic `quiz.json`. Keep old question ids. Leave HTML quiz runners, `postMessage`, and tracking unchanged. The combined S3 MCQ picker stays at `ch01-earth/worksheets/s3-mc`.

## HTML to keep

`content-packs/<pack>/tools/<slug>/index.html` and `content-packs/<pack>/worksheets/<slug>/index.html` (and their JS/CSS) — All-In-One embeds these.

## Stop

Duplicate `scope`, year-folder wrappers, topic-level pack splits, or quiz runner / tracking changes → ask the technical owner. Do not push.
